        setup: {
          players: 'Best with 2 players or 4 in partnerships.',
          deck: 'Standard 52-card deck. Ace = 1. Jacks/Queens/Kings have no numerical sum value (rank-only).',
          equipment: '',
          dealing: 'Each player receives 4 cards. 4 cards are placed face-up in the center field. The rest form a stock pile.',
          hasPlaceholders: false,
        },
        rules: {
          objective: "Score the most points by capturing specific 'score cards' and the largest volume of cards.",
          gameplay: '1. Play a card from hand to capture from the field.\n2. **Rank Match**: Match a Jack, Queen, King, or numeral rank to take it (e.g., King takes King).\n3. **Sum Match**: Use a numeral card (e.g., a 9) to take multiple cards whose values sum to it (e.g., 9 takes a 4, a 2, and an Ace (1)).\n4. **Discard**: If you cannot capture, leave your card on the table.\n5. When hands are empty, deal 4 more cards each from stock until the stock is gone.',
          keyRules: [
            'Capture by matching rank (e.g. 7 takes 7, Queen takes Queen) or by sum (numeral card takes cards summing to it; Ace = 1; face cards only match rank).',
            'If you cannot or do not wish to capture, play a card face up to the tableau (laying).',
            'When hands are empty, dealer deals 4 more cards each from the talon; no new cards to the tableau. Non-dealer plays first after each deal.',
            'Round ends when the last hand is played; remaining tableau cards go to the player who last made a capture.',
          ],
          hasPlaceholders: false,
        },
        strategy: {
          basic: "Prioritize capturing the **Ten of Diamonds** and the **Two of Clubs**. These cards count for points themselves and contribute to both the 'Most Cards' and 'Most Clubs' categories.",
          intermediate: "The 'Seven' Rule: Hold your middle-rank cards (5s, 6s, 7s). These are the most flexible for capturing combinations of low cards (Aces, 2s, 3s).",
          advanced: 'Last-Round Denial: If you know the stock is empty, try to be the last person to capture ANY card. The person who makes the last capture gets all the remaining cards on the table for free.',
          tips: [
            "Face cards (J, Q, K) are the easiest to track. If you see three Kings on the table, save your King for as long as possible to capture all four in one 'bomb'.",
            'Pay attention to the Clubs! Winning by just one Club can be the deciding factor in a close match.',
          ],
          hasPlaceholders: false,
        },
